\begin{proposition}[Role-Selective Differentiation on the Writable Tower]\label{prop:bridge-tower-differentiation}
For the two prepared role profiles, let $C_{pr}$ be the clean early-phase response to a probe of role $r$ after a reference write minus the response after a lesion, with one common sham between write and probe. With the declared probe at the transported address, $C_{pr}=\delta\mathbf 1_{\{p=r\}}$ for $\delta=1/(16\cdot3^7)$ turns. The best additive fit $a_p+b_r$ has uniform error exactly $\delta/2$. At error at most $\delta/16$ per phase reading the measured matrix still has distance at least $3\delta/8$ from all additive fits.
