The mixed difference $C_{00}-C_{01}-C_{10}+C_{11}=2\delta$ vanishes for every additive rival. An entrywise error of at most $e$ can change it by at most $4e$, giving $e\ge\delta/2$. The constant fit $\delta/2$ attains equality. Error in the measured paired contrast is at most $\delta/8$, so the triangle inequality gives the stated noisy lower bound. Two reference writes give zero contrast. A rival with the measured role-by-probe interaction can reproduce the clean matrix. This comparison identifies role-selective causal differentiation beyond the additive rival.
