\begin{proposition}[Late Choice Between Two Live Alternatives]\label{prop:bridge-tower-ambiguity}
Prepare two independent uniform activity bits at tape sites $3,4$ and advance one common sham. A uniform query drawn after the rival's memory is fixed selects one of the transported sites $4,5$. The matching-role probe identifies the selected bit with zero error at phase noise at most $\delta/16$. Under this state and query law the optimal error of a rival retaining one bit before the query, with no subsequent tape reading, is exactly $1/4$. A write during the advance can erase the first alternative while preserving the second.
